## 5. Unification and dao.jing.remote

**Sweep.** Every network primitive in `src/` was located by grep (`WebSocket|DatagramSocket|java.net|Socket|dgram|http-kit` etc.); the only dao/yin files touching sockets or HTTP are the four ws adapters, `dao.jing.dht/node.cljc`, `dao.jing.remote*`, `yin.repl*`, and the demos. Checked and correctly excluded from the fate table: `src/clj/world/server.clj` (website ring/httpkit server), `src/clj/world/datom/ollama.clj` (HTTP client to a local LLM — application tool, not a dao.stream path), `dao.stream.waitset*` (not network), `yin.repl.host*`/`embed`/`main`/`flutter` (the ws host seam, covered by the yin.repl row's URL item), demos (consumers; slice 5's proof names "the demo REPLs work"; `equation_plotter.cljs:233` uses `dao.stream.apply/call`, the AST node the fate row correctly keeps). `yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:370` mentions WS/UDP as examples only. **Nothing is missing from the table.**

